---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Grid from '../../components/Grid.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import Stats from '../../components/Stats.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Our Response"
  description="A permanent record of how the Florida Lantern Project responded to Hurricanes Helene, Milton, and Melissa — what we did, who we helped, and what it took."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Our response"
    title="What we did, storm by storm"
    lede="A permanent record rather than a feed. Each storm gets a page that stays up: what happened, what we did, who it reached, and what we'd do differently."
  />

  <Section>
    <Grid>
      <Card title="Hurricane Helene" href="/response/helene-2024" meta="September 2024">
        <p>
          The storm that changed what this organization does. We stepped outside
          our mission to provide urgent support, and never stepped back.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Hurricane Milton" href="/response/milton-2024" meta="October 2024">
        <p>
          Two weeks after Helene. Emergency lodging for more than 20 people,
          free phone plans, and dozens of roof inspections across Tampa Bay.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Hurricane Melissa" href="/response/melissa-2025" meta="2025 · concluded">
        <p>
          Lanterns for Jamaica — an effort to extend Florida's hurricane-tested
          compassion to the Caribbean. It did not reach the scale we hoped.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" title="The totals so far">
    <Stats />
  </Section>

  <Section title="Why these pages exist">
    <p>
      Most of what small nonprofits do disappears into social media, where it is
      unsearchable a week later and gone entirely if the platform decides so. A
      family looking for help next hurricane season can't find a Facebook post
      from 2024. Neither can a grantmaker.
    </p>
    <p>
      So we write it down here, where it stays.
    </p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
